      "behavior": "Expose the exact GUI/misc checkbox immediately after ISO-time preference. Typed default true, actual saved ClientOptions decoding, native override wins and retained legacy fallback for old imported stores. Options edits stage independently; Cancel/hidden/stale Apply do not write, changed Apply persists and unchanged Apply preserves newer saved values and other GUI fields. Every current native radio group reads live saved policy per Return: filesize, hash sign/type and advanced deletion action/reason. True uses explicit OK; false delegates to the actual parent default/button bubble. All40 actual modal Linux Qt cases accept, for both Enter/Return and all initial/live combinations; false is not promised to suppress dialog acceptance. Multiline hash text retains newline consumption. Captured pane index is armed by the focused radio and cleared on page navigation. Delete Return no longer captures before children; Escape and custom reason LineEdit behavior remain. Closed/hidden/retired child or parent cannot apply through either route.",
